  "question": {
    ":question/id": "9f378a65-9245-51ef-91d2-6d13f5890428",
    ":question/problem": "Find $AB$, if \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$\nand \n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$",
    ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
    ":question/worked-solution": "Here, $A$ is $3\\times 1$ matrix and $B$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere is $1$ column in matrix $A$ and $1$ row in matrix $B$, so the product is well defined:\n\n$$\n{A}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 2}={AB}_{3\\times 2}\n$$\n\nComputing the product, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2\\cdot (-7) & 2\\cdot 1 \\\\ 6\\cdot (-7) & 6\\cdot 1 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot (-7) & (-1)\\cdot 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-14 & 2 \\\\ -42 & 6 \\\\ 7 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
